hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27895","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Sharik ibn Ubaydillah informed us, from Jami' ibn Abi Rashid, from Mundhir al-Thawri, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali, he said: A woman of the Ansar narrated to me, and she is alive today; if you wish I shall admit you to her. I said: No. She said: I entered upon Umm Salamah, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon her as though angry. So I concealed myself with the sleeve of my garment. He spoke words I did not understand. So I said: O Mother of the Believers, it seemed I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, angry. She said: Yes, did you not hear him? She said: I said: And what did he say? She said: He said: When evil spreads in the land and is not forbidden, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, sends His punishment upon the people of the land. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, though among them are the righteous? He said: Yes, though among them are the righteous. What befell the people befalls them, then Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, takes them to His forgiveness and mercy, or to His mercy and forgiveness."
